Teleport-at-will has a criterion for triggering that is nothing to do
with having a ring or not.  You must have teleportation from any source,
be at least experience level 12 (8 if you are a wizard), or be
polymorphed into something that can teleport.  Alternatively, if you
know teleport away, ^T attempts to cast it if you are not confused but
you have failed the previous check.

If you pass the above checks, you must meet the following conditions in
order to actually teleport:

You must have at least 100 nutrition remaining, have a current strength
of 6 or greater, and have at least 20 energy (interestingly, the act
only actually *costs* 19 energy, but the check is "if (u.uen <= energy)"
where energy has been assigned a value that works out as 19.
